":"photo-16edeb6333e7831e4797","enabled":true,"image":{"src":"/reference-gallery/16edeb6333e7831e4797.webp","alt":"Stone garden basin amid tropical plants","category":"Spaces"},"width":549,"height":823,"viewerOrder":149,"categories":[]},{"id":"photo-722252c241ca10c517f7","enabled":true,"image":{"src":"/reference-gallery/722252c241ca10c517f7.webp","alt":"Sunrise silhouettes of palms and a beach visitor","category":"Spaces"},"width":549,"height":823,"viewerOrder":148,"categories":[]},{"id":"photo-b61e9790c80c034c2773","enabled":true,"image":{"src":"/reference-gallery/b61e9790c80c034c2773.webp","alt":"Living room with polished wood floor and open windows","category":"Spaces"},"width":549,"height":823,"viewerOrder":156,"categories":["bungalows"]},{"id":"photo-57ae197b044192338acf","enabled":true,"image":{"src":"/reference-gallery/57ae197b044192338acf.webp","alt":"Framed painting on a stone wall beside a palm","category":"Spaces"},"width":549,"height":823,"viewerOrder":154,"categories":[]}]},"amenities":["Private pool","Daily breakfast","Garden living","Thoughtful service","Fast Wi-Fi","Airport transfer"],"rooms":[{"id":"rooms-village-bungalow","slug":"village-bungalow","title":"Village Bungalow","description":"Our Village Bungalows, which comprise sixteen large, charming cottages, are some of the first structures designed by Pak Wija. They are inspired by traditional Balinese architecture, with a thatched roof and cool, air-conditioned interiors.","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/ec7335ef6b985507.webp","alt":"Village Bungalow","category":"Spaces"},"capacity":2,"area":45,"facilities":["Cotton shirt, sarong & sun hat","Bathub","Hairdryer","Minibar","Safety deposit box","Tea/coffee maker","Telephone","Wifi"],"inclusions":["Daily ala carte Breakfast in the seaside restaurant","Two bottles of water provided in the room complimentary  daily","Cold towel upon arrival","Welcome drink at the beachfront bar"],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-rooms/1cf3dd4a833ce838.webp","alt":"Village Bungalow exterior","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"Our Village Bungalows, which comprise sixteen large, charming cottages, are some of the first structures designed by Pak Wija. They are inspired by traditional Balinese architecture, with a thatched roof and cool, air-conditioned interiors.","body":["Each group of four bungalows is arranged in a configuration resembling the Hindu cosmic wheel, connected at the center to a vintage balé kulkul tower.   The spacious bedroom and living area includes a king-sized bed and two sofas that can convert into single beds. The large bathroom leads to an outdoor shower in a secluded courtyard garden. The outsized bathtub presides between the indoor and outdoor spaces. As you lie back and soak in the tub, you can gaze through the glass wall into your private garden and view Bali’s tropical sky.","All Village Bungalows are set within a landscaped garden, with a Balinese-style lounging pavilion or balé. The flooring features a variety of handmade ceramic tile types and colors, including red, blue, and terracotta batik tiles, alongside terrazzo flooring."],"showcase":{"wide":{"src":"/reference-rooms/b74dfb6ea4937b20.webp","alt":"Village Bungalow bedroom","category":"Spaces"},"small":{"src":"/reference-rooms/bab9c99758e81319.webp","alt":"Village Bungalow architectural detail","category":"Spaces"},"tall":{"src":"/reference-rooms/2cacc9efe2fe34c7.webp","alt":"Village Bungalow living space","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"Each room at Tandjung Sari has its own unique charm.","body":"The pictures depicted here illustrate the bungalow type mentioned, though you may book this bungalow type and experience a unit with slightly different attributes."},"gallery":[{"id":"photograph-1","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/6ca1d72b3a14640c.webp","alt":"Village Bungalow bath and courtyard","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-2","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/b0d387542915b5fb.webp","alt":"Village Bungalow bedroom and sitting area","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-3","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/056459f37aa38390.webp","alt":"Village Bungalow garden pavilion","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-4","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/5a0ce4c5054af599.webp","alt":"Village Bungalow interior living space","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-5","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/5d935dc09dd6b150.webp","alt":"Village Bungalow bathroom","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-6","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/86c038b9ea9bcf87.webp","alt":"Village Bungalow terrace","category":"Spaces"}}]}},{"id":"rooms-two-storey-bungalow","slug":"two-storey-bungalow","title":"Two-Storey Bungalow","description":"Tucked away in its own garden with a spacious terrace and polished wooden interiors.","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/8ef1d619416ca0d3.webp","alt":"Two-Storey Bungalow","category":"Spaces"},"capacity":2,"area":50,"facilities":["Cotton shirt, sarong & sun hat","Bathub","Hairdryer","Minibar","Safety deposit box","Tea/Coffee Maker","Telephone","Wifi"],"inclusions":["Daily ala carte Breakfast in the seaside restaurant","Two bottles of water provided in the room complimentary daily","Cold towel upon arrival","Welcome drink at the beachfront bar"],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-rooms/8ef1d619416ca0d3.webp","alt":"Two-Storey Bungalow exterior","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"Our four two-storey bungalows are tucked away, each in its own gardens. Each bungalow has a spacious terrace and polished wooden interiors.","body":["Step up to the upper-level living areas, which have windows on three sides, maximizing natural light and garden views.  The ground floor—three units with polished timber floors and the other one with terrazzo tiles—houses a queen-sized canopied bed and a bathroom complete with a handmade terrazzo tub, big enough for two.","Exposed brick, a quirky stone relief, and the antique carved wooden door and windows visually enrich the veranda, which frames a serene private garden."],"showcase":{"wide":{"src":"/reference-rooms/c66840c00ba7f017.webp","alt":"Two-Storey Bungalow bedroom","category":"Spaces"},"small":{"src":"/reference-rooms/1b0f72cae92311be.webp","alt":"Two-Storey Bungalow architectural detail","category":"Spaces"},"tall":{"src":"/reference-rooms/aa3f826d15d55a73.webp","alt":"Two-Storey Bungalow living space","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"Each room at Tandjung Sari has its own unique charm.","body":"The pictures depicted here illustrate the bungalow type mentioned, though you may book this bungalow type and experience a unit with slightly different attributes."},"gallery":[{"id":"photograph-1","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/ff894b463c129757.webp","alt":"Two-Storey Bungalow bath and courtyard","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-2","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/61bd4d69a6f267a0.webp","alt":"Two-Storey Bungalow bedroom and sitting area","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-3","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/a315917ce861decc.webp","alt":"Two-Storey Bungalow garden pavilion","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-4","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/00a489def911becd.webp","alt":"Two-Storey Bungalow interior living space","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-5","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/a0f5a09a8779ad3c.webp","alt":"Two-Storey Bungalow bathroom","category":"Spaces"}}]}},{"id":"rooms-beachfront-bungalow","slug":"beachfront-bungalow","title":"Beachfront Bungalow","description":"Nestled in a beachside garden, this cozy retreat offers sea views from an upstairs loft.","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/4f9f73343b2638ac.webp","alt":"Beachfront Bungalow","category":"Spaces"},"capacity":2,"area":55,"facilities":["Cotton shirt, sarong & sun hat","Bathub","Hairdryer","Minibar","Safety deposit box","Tea/Coffee Maker","Telephone","Wifi"],"inclusions":["Daily ala carte Breakfast in the seaside restaurant","Two bottles of water provided in the room complimentary daily","Cold towel upon arrival","Welcome drink at the beachfront bar"],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-rooms/c53a8138d8de844b.webp","alt":"Beachfront Bungalow exterior","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"Discover the barefoot glamour of our two sanctuaries closest to the beach.","body":["The façade reflects the beauty of traditional Balinese architecture, set within a flourishing beachside courtyard, while the hardwood and bamboo materials deepen your connection to nature. You enter the ground-floor bedroom—one bungalow with a wooden floor and the other with terracotta tile—through an antique Balinese doorway.","The ground floor also features an indoor bathroom and an outdoor shower.  Ascend the spiral staircase to the upper level, where you’ll feel embraced by the treetops. The classic veranda invites you to unwind and enjoy the sights and sounds of the seaside garden."],"showcase":{"wide":{"src":"/reference-rooms/0420b46dffa9e3d8.webp","alt":"Beachfront Bungalow bedroom","category":"Spaces"},"small":{"src":"/reference-rooms/602538ad829201de.webp","alt":"Beachfront Bungalow architectural detail","category":"Spaces"},"tall":{"src":"/reference-rooms/6adff473b5bd13bc.webp","alt":"Beachfront Bungalow living space","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"Each room at Tandjung Sari has its own unique charm.","body":"The pictures depicted here illustrate the bungalow type mentioned, though you may book this bungalow type and experience a unit with slightly different attributes."},"gallery":[{"id":"photograph-1","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/915686a353285631.webp","alt":"Beachfront Bungalow bath and courtyard","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-2","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/4c4d8ad6c46f0060.webp","alt":"Beachfront Bungalow bedroom and sitting area","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-3","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/9dab833fe1a11072.webp","alt":"Beachfront Bungalow garden pavilion","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-4","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/4af3e7415895ec81.webp","alt":"Beachfront Bungalow interior living space","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-5","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/88fc45a60c9a34d9.webp","alt":"Beachfront Bungalow bathroom","category":"Spaces"}}]}},{"id":"rooms-south-garden-bungalow","slug":"south-garden-bungalow","title":"South Garden Bungalow","description":"The spacious bedroom with canopied queen bed has a large work table and a day bed, ideal for reading.","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/37ad0a13d67c51f6.webp","alt":"South Garden Bungalow","category":"Spaces"},"capacity":2,"area":128,"facilities":["Cotton shirt, sarong & sun hat","Bathub","Hairdryer","Minibar","Safety deposit box","Tea/Coffee Maker","Telephone","Wifi"],"inclusions":["Daily ala carte Breakfast in the seaside restaurant","Two bottles of water provided in the room complimentary daily","Cold towel upon arrival","Welcome drink at the beachfront bar"],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-rooms/37ad0a13d67c51f6.webp","alt":"South Garden Bungalow exterior","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"The four inviting units of the South Garden Bungalows are a new generation of bungalows with traditional roofs and sleek interiors—a descriptive intersection between vintage and modern.","body":["Two bungalows boast thatched roofs adorned with blue batik tiles and outdoor bathtubs, while the others feature wood shingle roofs complemented by green celadon batik tiles and indoor bathtubs. Stroll through the gardens and discover the traditionally proportioned veranda, graced with carved wooden pillars, a kamasan painting, and carefully curated antique windows and doors—each element profoundly telling a story of the Tandjung Sari experience.","Inside, spacious bedrooms welcome you with a canopied queen bed, a generous work table and a daybed, ideal for reading. Each bungalow offers a decent bathroom and dressing area, equipped with twin vanity sinks, double wardrobe closets, and an indoor shower with seating. Step beyond the door to uncover an outdoor shower with a refreshing rain showerhead."],"showcase":{"wide":{"src":"/reference-rooms/32e09ec5f44e03cd.webp","alt":"South Garden Bungalow bedroom","category":"Spaces"},"small":{"src":"/reference-rooms/c918e73a55924d26.webp","alt":"South Garden Bungalow architectural detail","category":"Spaces"},"tall":{"src":"/reference-rooms/f855bc9c1e6649eb.webp","alt":"South Garden Bungalow living space","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"Each room at Tandjung Sari has its own unique charm.","body":"The pictures depicted here illustrate the bungalow type mentioned, though you may book this bungalow type and experience a unit with slightly different attributes."},"gallery":[{"id":"photograph-1","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/63dd944a232d9ee5.webp","alt":"South Garden Bungalow bath and courtyard","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-2","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/ac796aeefb254c6f.webp","alt":"South Garden Bungalow bedroom and sitting area","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-3","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/bb008ddbb7268e74.webp","alt":"South Garden Bungalow garden pavilion","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-4","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/9b51273f484e109a.webp","alt":"South Garden Bungalow interior living space","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-5","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/5c374843b8fd1a6c.webp","alt":"South Garden Bungalow bathroom","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-6","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/f24d883d475f62e9.webp","alt":"South Garden Bungalow terrace","category":"Spaces"}}]}},{"id":"rooms-garden-seaview-bungalow","slug":"garden-seaview-bungalow","title":"Garden Seaview Bungalow","description":"Charming bungalow in a secluded garden, with a spacious veranda and views to the sea.","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/50294ef5a663cd15.webp","alt":"Garden Seaview Bungalow","category":"Spaces"},"capacity":2,"area":70,"facilities":["Cotton shirt, sarong & sun hat","Bathub","Hairdryer","Minibar","Safety deposit box","Tea/Coffee maker","Telephone","Wifi"],"inclusions":["Daily ala carte Breakfast in the seaside restaurant","Two bottles of water provided in the room complimentary daily","Cold towel upon arrival","Welcome drink at the beachfront bar"],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-rooms/50294ef5a663cd15.webp","alt":"Garden Seaview Bungalow exterior","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"Explore and encounter the soul of the Garden Seaview Bungalow #24 — a unique bungalow with its own secluded leafy garden, spacious airy veranda, and front-on-ocean vistas.","body":["This bungalow captivates with its antique entry door. As you enter, you will be delighted with the warmth of the terracotta-colored batik tiles. Further, you will notice the ivory oval indoor bathtub complemented by an indoor shower and a classic modern dressing table.","The backyard features a tropical outdoor shower, for bathing in the midst of nature. Each carefully curated piece of furniture, artwork, and ornament infuses the space with a quiet spell."],"showcase":{"wide":{"src":"/reference-rooms/75604cc478c7e300.webp","alt":"Garden Seaview Bungalow bedroom","category":"Spaces"},"small":{"src":"/reference-rooms/74b7782a47890edd.webp","alt":"Garden Seaview Bungalow architectural detail","category":"Spaces"},"tall":{"src":"/reference-rooms/8d8a081dcc581a90.webp","alt":"Garden Seaview Bungalow living space","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"Each room at Tandjung Sari has its own unique charm.","body":"The pictures depicted here illustrate the bungalow type mentioned, though you may book this bungalow type and experience a unit with slightly different attributes."},"gallery":[{"id":"photograph-1","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/8059441e5e122b08.webp","alt":"Garden Seaview Bungalow bath and courtyard","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-2","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/19629064fd905164.webp","alt":"Garden Seaview Bungalow bedroom and sitting area","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-3","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/8a365dacce5af6af.webp","alt":"Garden Seaview Bungalow garden pavilion","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-4","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/2679a71afa843ae2.webp","alt":"Garden Seaview Bungalow interior living space","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-5","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/c09d6c04ed64fffc.webp","alt":"Garden Seaview Bungalow bathroom","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-6","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/4f6a3ae37818944d.webp","alt":"Garden Seaview Bungalow terrace","category":"Spaces"}}]}},{"id":"rooms-family-bungalow","slug":"family-bungalow","title":"Family Bungalow","description":"The Family Bungalows are designed to provide a cozy getaway for families in Sanur, offering comfort and tranquility with interconnected sleeping areas, terraces, and gardens. Each bungalow features two bedrooms: one with a queen-sized bed and another with two twin beds.","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/23cc47b4582b9331.webp","alt":"Family Bungalow","category":"Spaces"},"capacity":4,"area":135,"facilities":["Cotton shirt, sarong & sun hat","Bathub","Hairdryer","Minibar","Safety deposit box","Tea/Coffee Maker","Telephone","Wifi"],"inclusions":["Daily ala carte Breakfast in the seaside restaurant","Two bottles of water provided in the room complimentary daily","Cold towel upon arrival","Welcome drink at the beachfront bar"],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-rooms/4ad25185c5b1d69a.webp","alt":"Family Bungalow exterior","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"The Family Bungalows are designed to provide a cozy getaway for families in Sanur, offering comfort and tranquility with interconnected sleeping areas, terraces, and gardens.","body":["Each bungalow features two bedrooms: one with a queen-sized bed and another with two twin beds. These rooms embody the unique style of Tandjung Sari while showcasing their own individual character.","As you approach the bungalows, you will notice a Kamasan painting displayed above the door. Inside, the bungalows are adorned with a light green color scheme and batik floor tiles. Each bungalow also includes a family bathtub overlooking the backyard garden, along with outdoor showers."],"showcase":{"wide":{"src":"/reference-rooms/5019670d82b75845.webp","alt":"Family Bungalow bedroom","category":"Spaces"},"small":{"src":"/reference-rooms/6bcbcf2239194086.webp","alt":"Family Bungalow architectural detail","category":"Spaces"},"tall":{"src":"/reference-rooms/bf121188e08e15d3.webp","alt":"Family Bungalow living space","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"Each room at Tandjung Sari has its own unique charm.","body":"The pictures depicted here illustrate the bungalow type mentioned, though you may book this bungalow type and experience a unit with slightly different attributes."},"gallery":[{"id":"photograph-1","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/7ebd7680a137cf0a.webp","alt":"Family Bungalow bath and courtyard","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-2","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/2ebac394a22d2490.webp","alt":"Family Bungalow bedroom and sitting area","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-3","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/5b8285feef0af434.webp","alt":"Family Bungalow garden pavilion","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"photograph-4","image":{"src":"/reference-rooms/f5adda664a784d5e.webp","alt":"Family Bungalow interior living space","category":"Spaces"}}]}}],"signatureRooms":{"title":"Our Rooms","hero":{"src":"/reference-story/hero-image-bungalow-resizedjpg.jpeg","alt":"Aerial photograph of Tandjung Sari bungalows","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"Tandjung Sari is a handmade resort. The resorts \"rooms\" are stand-alone cottages—always called bungalows—set in walled gardens.","smallImage":{"src":"/reference-rooms/df530c83448f8ad2.webp","alt":"Handmade Village Bungalow interior","category":"Spaces"},"smallCopy":"Local craftsmen constructed them organically, showcasing the resort's distinctive handmade character in its architecture, interiors, and furnishings.","largeImage":{"src":"/reference-rooms/05367bbc53f7f29a.webp","alt":"Traditional carved gateway at Tandjung Sari","category":"Spaces"},"largeCopy":"These bungalows are thoughtfully placed throughout the property and were beautifully designed based on a sketch by the founder, Wija Wawo-Runtu.","ornament":{"src":"/reference-rooms/listing-ornament.svg","alt":"Coral ornament","category":"Spaces"}},"modules":{"dining":true,"experiences":true,"packages":true,"terms":true},"dining":{"title":"Culinary","description":"The Restaurant at Tandjung Sari offers you more than a seaside dining experience. You may choose to dine in the airy wantilan pavilion amongst Indonesian antiques or on the wooden deck under the shady camplung trees near the bar area, right on Sanur Beach. Our homemade cuisine reflects our passion for authentic local and international food, accompanied by specially crafted drinks. Open every day, from 6.30am to 11pm.","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/a0cdcf1d52648a3898dc.webp","alt":"Dining illustrated Balinese village","category":"Spaces"},"bookingUrl":"https://example.com/dining","signature":{"introTitle":"The Restaurant at Tandjung Sari","categories":[{"id":"breakfast","enabled":true,"title":"Breakfast","description":"Sanur, the \"Morning of the World,\" unveils a breathtaking moment when the sun rises, casting a golden glow on the sand and igniting the sky with color—a true masterpiece of nature. There are countless ways to start the day, but is there a better way than to savor breakfast while witnessing a natural wonder?","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/08038031e1c9a5f9d48f.webp","alt":"Breakfast","category":"Spaces"},"menuPages":[{"id":"breakfast-page-1","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/2a40a45176a72df0f947.webp","alt":"Breakfast menu page 1","category":"Spaces"},"width":2044,"height":2892},{"id":"breakfast-page-2","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/326fb61058fa95492bbd.webp","alt":"Breakfast menu page 2","category":"Spaces"},"width":2044,"height":2892},{"id":"breakfast-page-3","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/5a5b0cb2e49bf92bfa58.webp","alt":"Breakfast menu page 3","category":"Spaces"},"width":2044,"height":2892}],"mobileMenuPages":[{"id":"breakfast-mobile-page-1","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/2a40a45176a72df0f947.webp","alt":"Breakfast mobile menu page 1","category":"Spaces"},"width":2044,"height":2892},{"id":"breakfast-mobile-page-2","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/6b7994f03543d42c649a.webp","alt":"Breakfast mobile menu page 2","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"breakfast-mobile-page-3","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/12c2f1dad84004dcf165.webp","alt":"Breakfast mobile menu page 3","category":"Spaces"},"width":1911,"height":3100},{"id":"breakfast-mobile-page-4","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/ac51c616c72b18737e62.webp","alt":"Breakfast mobile menu page 4","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"breakfast-mobile-page-5","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/466218676adaad5b0931.webp","alt":"Breakfast mobile menu page 5","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550}],"downloadUrl":""},{"id":"all-day-dining","enabled":true,"title":"All Day Dining","description":"Ever since our founder established Tandjung Sari as a family home, food has held equal importance to accommodation. Today, we continue to uphold the principles of home cooking. Created from fresh, locally grown produce and ingredients, we offer signature authentic local and international cuisine.","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/bb606c5e0861898c03c3.webp","alt":"All Day Dining","category":"Spaces"},"menuPages":[{"id":"all-day-dining-page-1","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/19fb1a774784a436926c.webp","alt":"All Day Dining menu page 1","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446},{"id":"all-day-dining-page-2","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/d1c764ed999f94b20b48.webp","alt":"All Day Dining menu page 2","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446},{"id":"all-day-dining-page-3","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/d5ecbf5b29ee1be7f2d1.webp","alt":"All Day Dining menu page 3","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446},{"id":"all-day-dining-page-4","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/396db0c7f2d9b6854ed3.webp","alt":"All Day Dining menu page 4","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446}],"mobileMenuPages":[{"id":"all-day-dining-mobile-page-1","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/4a2e0e638209b074b832.webp","alt":"All Day Dining mobile menu page 1","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"all-day-dining-mobile-page-2","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/7ae21801d46892e134ca.webp","alt":"All Day Dining mobile menu page 2","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"all-day-dining-mobile-page-3","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/1d80ffc9713f056df173.webp","alt":"All Day Dining mobile menu page 3","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"all-day-dining-mobile-page-4","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/0a520d9884f1a4026d4a.webp","alt":"All Day Dining mobile menu page 4","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"all-day-dining-mobile-page-5","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/98fe51403f3f25d94205.webp","alt":"All Day Dining mobile menu page 5","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"all-day-dining-mobile-page-6","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/0fcf9ed4a8a21170fd69.webp","alt":"All Day Dining mobile menu page 6","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550}],"downloadUrl":""},{"id":"drinks","enabled":true,"title":"Drinks & Wines","description":"Tandjung Sari's beachfront bar is the ultimate place to gather at all hours of the day. The bar menu offers a hand-picked selection of refreshments with fresh tropical flavors—whether soft, sweet, or a bit stronger. Contact us to explore our selection of wines and take advantage of special offers designed for wine enthusiasts.","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/2486277bb07cc788020e.webp","alt":"Drinks & Wines","category":"Spaces"},"menuPages":[{"id":"drinks-page-1","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/f7c87a41940942f0d53e.webp","alt":"Drinks menu page 1","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446},{"id":"drinks-page-2","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/b8832502fd02e55e5ecc.webp","alt":"Drinks menu page 2","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446},{"id":"drinks-page-3","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/4dafd3a63b5d8d1d342c.webp","alt":"Drinks menu page 3","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446},{"id":"drinks-page-4","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/edbf639be2ea6f666460.webp","alt":"Drinks menu page 4","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446},{"id":"drinks-page-5","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/c1fde131d877e164cce8.webp","alt":"Drinks menu page 5","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446},{"id":"drinks-page-6","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/00a6b49c253d0ed50286.webp","alt":"Drinks menu page 6","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446},{"id":"drinks-page-7","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/73f241b2151b03d72e65.webp","alt":"Drinks menu page 7","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446},{"id":"drinks-page-8","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/f3a89616869e4cd06694.webp","alt":"Drinks menu page 8","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446},{"id":"drinks-page-9","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/6a96f390a219c9dbdd43.webp","alt":"Drinks menu page 9","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446},{"id":"drinks-page-10","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/c4792e060ed6e38f72a4.webp","alt":"Drinks menu page 10","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446},{"id":"drinks-page-11","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/fa3b0b775885e29148f5.webp","alt":"Drinks menu page 11","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446},{"id":"drinks-page-12","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/d1bf2a5d20747b3017ae.webp","alt":"Drinks menu page 12","category":"Spaces"},"width":1022,"height":1446}],"mobileMenuPages":[{"id":"drinks-mobile-page-1","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/6233954714a7c9b4b398.webp","alt":"Drinks mobile menu page 1","category":"Spaces"},"width":1333,"height":2162},{"id":"drinks-mobile-page-2","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/ddd44badb92cdf061c53.webp","alt":"Drinks mobile menu page 2","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"drinks-mobile-page-3","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/2ed1cb1d7af497c08ff8.webp","alt":"Drinks mobile menu page 3","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"drinks-mobile-page-4","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/a82d5dd4941630f1d0eb.webp","alt":"Drinks mobile menu page 4","category":"Spaces"},"width":956,"height":1550},{"id":"drinks-mobile-page-5","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/85657d4d01707b3da509.webp","alt":"Drinks mobile menu page 5","category":"Spaces"},"width":956,"height":1550},{"id":"drinks-mobile-page-6","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/f57811019926fe19f25d.webp","alt":"Drinks mobile menu page 6","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"drinks-mobile-page-7","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/95f462e051d329d0ae36.webp","alt":"Drinks mobile menu page 7","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"drinks-mobile-page-8","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/d56ac82bf1acc8b59fb7.webp","alt":"Drinks mobile menu page 8","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"drinks-mobile-page-9","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/e578710cf00d2db7d421.webp","alt":"Drinks mobile menu page 9","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"drinks-mobile-page-10","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/a5c5125038a9b11d6cc5.webp","alt":"Drinks mobile menu page 10","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"drinks-mobile-page-11","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/3924eff6e62f59e5abc5.webp","alt":"Drinks mobile menu page 11","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"drinks-mobile-page-12","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/3924eff6e62f59e5abc5.webp","alt":"Drinks mobile menu page 12","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550},{"id":"drinks-mobile-page-13","image":{"src":"/reference-dining/4ac27e5a23ed5463d7d8.webp","alt":"Drinks mobile menu page 13","category":"Spaces"},"width":955,"height":1550}],"downloadUrl":""}],"offers":[{"id":"afternoon-tea","enabled":true,"title":"Afternoon Tea","description":["Relishing tea is a deep, personal ritual that allows one to connect with oneself and life's moments. Offered in Indonesian style, we invite you to wind up your afternoon luxuriating in an assortment of sweet and savory local traditional jajan presented on a three-tier stand.","Please note that a one-day advance booking is essential."],"image":{"src":"/reference-dining/4ccc3453e11a97ce2776.webp","alt":"Afternoon Tea","category":"Spaces"},"reservationUrl":""},{"id":"mini-rijsttafel","enabled":true,"title":"Mini Rijsttafel","description":["The traditional rijsttafel is a study of Indonesian regional dishes and Balinese flair for presentation. It features a vast array of local fare to accompany rice—fish, fowl, beef, eggs, and vegetables, each prepared in varied ways to highlight rich flavor, color, and texture.","Perfect for two."],"image":{"src":"/reference-dining/a15b21f409205ab46a0e.webp","alt":"Mini Rijsttafel","category":"Spaces"},"reservationUrl":""},{"id":"private-gathering","enabled":true,"title":"Private Gathering","description":["For 10 people or more.","Serene Sanur Beach in the Tandjung Sari style creates an idyllic place for being together. If you prefer a more tailored dining experience to gather with your loved ones, we would be delighted to accommodate you.","Choose from one of our beachside living room areas and enjoy a selection of home-cooked dishes and refreshments."],"image":{"src":"/reference-dining/fa74697b9cc345db1d45.webp","alt":"Private Gathering","category":"Spaces"},"reservationUrl":""},{"id":"romantic-dinner","enabled":true,"title":"Romantic Dinner","description":["We believe in the magic of crafting happy memories. Tandjung Sari's\nintimate beachside dinner offers specially arranged four-course options\ncomplemented with a bottle of house wine. The ambiance is enriched with fresh\ntropical flowers, setting the stage for a memorable experience."],"image":{"src":"/reference-dining/237b43813aef982de60e.webp","alt":"Romantic Dinner","category":"Spaces"},"reservationUrl":""}],"notes":["Vegan","Vegetarian by Request","If you have any dietary restrictions or allergies, please inform the order taker.","All prices are in thousands of Indonesian Rupiah and 21% government tax and service charge to be added."]}},"experiences":[{"id":"experiences-island-mornings","slug":"island-mornings","title":"Island mornings","description":"Follow the paths through green rice fields and discover a quieter side of Bali. Ask your host about a personal itinerary.","image":{"src":"/images/nature.jpg","alt":"Sunlight over a Balinese landscape","category":"Nature"}},{"id":"experiences-by-the-sea","slug":"by-the-sea","title":"A day by the sea","description":"Salt in the air, sand beneath your feet. Take the scenic route to the coast and leave the afternoon open.","image":{"src":"/images/beach.jpg","alt":"A quiet tropical shoreline under a blue sky","category":"Nature"}}],"packages":[{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon","enabled":true,"slug":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon","title":"Seaside Wedding & Honeymoon","description":"Celebrate and reignite your romance with a three-night stay, highlighted by a magical candlelit dinner on the beach.","image":{"src":"/reference-packages/1c8f518892c6a160ce56.webp","alt":"Seaside Wedding & Honeymoon reference photograph","category":"Living","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"signature":{"destination":"detail","enquiry":{"type":"external","url":"https://example.com/"},"referenceDemo":true,"sections":[{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-introduction","enabled":true,"layout":"intro","heading":"Love flourishes on the enchanting island of Bali, where the serene beauty of the Tandjung Sari seaside offers an unforgettable escape for honeymooners.","stayInfo":"Two nights stay at Village Bungalow for bride & groom","price":{"label":"Start From","currency":"IDR","amount":49410,"display":"IDR 49,410 for 20 guests","guestCount":20},"durationNights":2,"body":[],"small":{"src":"/reference-packages/e9dbcc2476af045a25a6.webp","alt":"Seaside Wedding & Honeymoon ceremonial detail","category":"Living","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"wide":{"src":"/reference-packages/38113a72a0b4b47fcdad.webp","alt":"Seaside Wedding & Honeymoon supporting photograph","category":"Living","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}}},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-rows-0","enabled":true,"layout":"inclusions","title":"Package Inclusion","entries":[{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-1","enabled":true,"text":"Five hours exclusive use of wedding venue: beach Area and few other optional areas"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-2","enabled":true,"text":"Buffet wedding dinner for 20 people with standard dinner set from selected menu"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-3","enabled":true,"text":"Twenty chairs with small cornflower shower"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-4","enabled":true,"text":"Traditional Balinese Rindik music during your ceremony"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-5","enabled":true,"text":"Four-poster bamboo gate with Balinese decoration"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-6","enabled":true,"text":"An altar table with flower arrangements"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-7","enabled":true,"text":"Six white flags of umbul-umbul"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-8","enabled":true,"text":"Four tall white Balinese umbrellas"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-9","enabled":true,"text":"Twenty decorative candles in the banana trunk cover"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-10","enabled":true,"text":"Four standing tropical flower arrangements"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-11","enabled":true,"text":"2000pcs virginal walk of flower petals"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-12","enabled":true,"text":"A standard tropical flower bridal bouquet"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-13","enabled":true,"text":"Two standard tropical flower buttonhole corsages"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-14","enabled":true,"text":"Twice glasses of house-local sparkling wine"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-15","enabled":true,"text":"One glass of mocktail upon guest arrival at the wedding venue"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-16","enabled":true,"text":"Two nights stay at Village Bungalow for bride & groom, inclusive of daily breakfast"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-17","enabled":true,"text":"A romantic dinner for the couple featuring one bottle of house-imported red or white wine"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-18","enabled":true,"text":"Wedding amenities in the Bungalow"},{"id":"seaside-wedding-and-honeymoon-row-0-19","enabled":true,"text":"21% government tax and service charge included"}]}]}},{"id":"hideaway-stay","enabled":true,"slug":"hideaway-stay","title":"Hideaway stay","description":"Reconnect with the soothing sea breeze and let the gentle waves of Sanur Beach nourish your body, mind, and spirit.","image":{"src":"/reference-packages/32032341633a0e03556f.webp","alt":"Hideaway stay reference photograph","category":"Living","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"signature":{"destination":"detail","enquiry":{"type":"external","url":"https://example.com/"},"referenceDemo":true,"sections":[{"id":"hideaway-stay-introduction","enabled":true,"layout":"intro","heading":"Embrace the opportunity to escape the everyday and indulge in a three-day, two-night stay at our seaside sanctuary.","stayInfo":"3d/2n stay in a Village Bungalow","price":{"label":"Start From","currency":"IDR","amount":8740000,"display":"Rp. 8.740.000"},"durationNights":2,"body":[],"small":{"src":"/reference-packages/fa3d6bc2e5bad81e3de4.webp","alt":"Hideaway stay ceremonial detail","category":"Living","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"wide":{"src":"/reference-packages/4ce6c61e028441f74921.webp","alt":"Hideaway stay supporting photograph","category":"Living","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}}},{"id":"hideaway-stay-rows-0","enabled":true,"layout":"inclusions","title":"Package Inclusion","entries":[{"id":"hideaway-stay-row-0-1","enabled":true,"text":"3d/2n stay in a Village Bungalow"},{"id":"hideaway-stay-row-0-2","enabled":true,"text":"Return airport transfer"},{"id":"hideaway-stay-row-0-3","enabled":true,"text":"Cold towel upon arrival"},{"id":"hideaway-stay-row-0-4","enabled":true,"text":"Welcome drink at the beachfront bar"},{"id":"hideaway-stay-row-0-5","enabled":true,"text":"Two complimentary bottles of mineral water daily in your room"},{"id":"hideaway-stay-row-0-6","enabled":true,"text":"Daily à la carte breakfast at the seaside restaurant"},{"id":"hideaway-stay-row-0-7","enabled":true,"text":"Complimentary use of a cotton shirt, sunhat, and sarong during your stay"},{"id":"hideaway-stay-row-0-8","enabled":true,"text":"Free internet access"},{"id":"hideaway-stay-row-0-9","enabled":true,"text":"Applicable government tax and service charge (21% included)"}]},{"id":"hideaway-stay-rows-1","enabled":true,"layout":"terms","title":"Bungalow upgrade additional charge","entries":[{"id":"hideaway-stay-row-1-1","enabled":true,"text":"IDR 300.000/night for Two Storey/Garden Sea View"},{"id":"hideaway-stay-row-1-2","enabled":true,"text":"IDR 600.000/night for Beach Bungalow"},{"id":"hideaway-stay-row-1-3","enabled":true,"text":"IDR 1,500,000/night for South Garden Bungalow"}]}]}},{"id":"stay-and-dine","enabled":true,"slug":"stay-and-dine","title":"Stay & Dine","description":"Experience Sanur's unpretentious hidden gem with its gentle sound of the sea in the culinary adventure of Tandjung Sari's signature Mini Rijsttafel dinner for two.","image":{"src":"/reference-packages/150765138429244c6e40.webp","alt":"Stay & Dine reference photograph","category":"Living","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"signature":{"destination":"detail","enquiry":{"type":"external","url":"https://example.com/"},"referenceDemo":true,"sections":[{"id":"stay-and-dine-introduction","enabled":true,"layout":"intro","heading":"This four-day, three-night experience is crafted for passionate travelers and food lovers alike.","stayInfo":"4D/3N stay at Village Bungalow","durationNights":3,"body":[],"small":{"src":"/reference-packages/606829a36af98f81f8ed.webp","alt":"Stay & Dine ceremonial detail","category":"Living","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"wide":{"src":"/reference-packages/3d726de09a9357287586.webp","alt":"Stay & Dine supporting photograph","category":"Living","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}}},{"id":"stay-and-dine-rows-0","enabled":true,"layout":"inclusions","title":"Package Inclusion","entries":[{"id":"stay-and-dine-row-0-1","enabled":true,"text":"4D/3N stay at Village Bungalow"},{"id":"stay-and-dine-row-0-2","enabled":true,"text":"Return airport transfer"},{"id":"stay-and-dine-row-0-3","enabled":true,"text":"1x  Mini Rijsttafel for 2 person"},{"id":"stay-and-dine-row-0-4","enabled":true,"text":"Cold towel upon arrival"},{"id":"stay-and-dine-row-0-5","enabled":true,"text":"Welcome drink at the beachfront bar"},{"id":"stay-and-dine-row-0-6","enabled":true,"text":"Two bottles of mineral water provided in the room complimentary daily"},{"id":"stay-and-dine-row-0-7","enabled":true,"text":"Daily ala carte breakfast in the seaside restaurant"},{"id":"stay-and-dine-row-0-8","enabled":true,"text":"Free usage of a cotton shirt, sunhat, and sarong during the stay"},{"id":"stay-and-dine-row-0-9","enabled":true,"text":"Free internet access"},{"id":"stay-and-dine-row-0-10","enabled":true,"text":"Applicable government tax and service charge (21% included)"}]},{"id":"stay-and-dine-rows-1","enabled":true,"layout":"terms","title":"Bungalow upgrade additional charge","entries":[{"id":"stay-and-dine-row-1-1","enabled":true,"text":"IDR 300.000/night at Two Storey/Garden Sea View"},{"id":"stay-and-dine-row-1-2","enabled":true,"text":"IDR 600.000/night at Beach Bungalow"},{"id":"stay-and-dine-row-1-3","enabled":true,"text":"IDR 1.500.000/night at South Garden Bungalow"}]}]}},{"id":"cooking-class","enabled":true,"slug":"cooking-class","title":"Cooking Class","description":"Discover the secrets of authentic Indonesian home-cooking while explore the exotic ingredients with traditional cooking techniques by our Chef.","image":{"src":"/reference-packages/cf846de2d8cc02de3eb6.webp","alt":"Cooking Class reference photograph","category":"Living","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"signature":{"destination":"enquiry","enquiry":{"type":"external","url":"https://example.com/"},"referenceDemo":true,"sections":[]}},{"id":"kado-gift-shop","enabled":true,"slug":"kado-gift-shop","title":"Kado Gift Shop","description":"Our boutique, Kado (meaning 'gift'), highlights Bali's finest artisans. Many homewares in your bungalow are available for purchase here, along with curated fashion items, jewelry, and books.","image":{"src":"/reference-packages/506cb9d8495c5dcd7434.webp","alt":"Kado Gift Shop reference photograph","category":"Living","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"signature":{"destination":"enquiry","enquiry":{"type":"external","url":"https://example.com/"},"referenceDemo":true,"sections":[]}}],"signatureLocation":{"id":"getting-here-editorial","enabled":true,"title":"Getting Here","description":"Tandjung Sari is located in the center of Sanur, offering convenient access to the airport and other destinations in Bali.","hero":{"src":"/reference-location/2ff0014d03d7f4a75e64.webp","alt":"Aerial view of Tandjung Sari gardens and winding paths","category":"Nature","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"heading":"Tandjung Sari is located in the center of Sanur, offering convenient access to the airport and other destinations in Bali.","contacts":{"phone":{"enabled":true,"label":"Phone","display":"+62 361 288441","number":"+62361288441"},"email":{"enabled":true,"label":"Mail","address":"info@tandjungsarihotel.com"},"address":{"enabled":true,"label":"Location","lines":["Jalan Danau Tamblingan No. 41 Sanur, Denpasar - 80228 Bali, Indonesia"]}},"small":{"src":"/reference-location/7f78d66f19cbad109402.webp","alt":"Tandjung Sari entrance gate surrounded by tropical plants","category":"Nature","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"map":{"src":"/reference-location/b48259c1ac530ff8e34d.webp","alt":"Static Sanur street map with the Tandjung Sari marker near the coast","category":"Nature","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"directionsUrl":"https://maps.app.goo.gl/5KhdAD7hAERJsFAX9","destinations":[{"id":"destination-1","enabled":true,"name":"Bali International Hospital","distance":"2.1 km"},{"id":"destination-2","enabled":true,"name":"Sanur Harbour","distance":"5.6 km"},{"id":"destination-3","enabled":true,"name":"Art Center","distance":"6.3 km"},{"id":"destination-4","enabled":true,"name":"Benoa Harbour","distance":"11 km"},{"id":"destination-5","enabled":true,"name":"Bali Ngurah Rai Airport","distance":"16 km"},{"id":"destination-6","enabled":true,"name":"Tanjung Benoa","distance":"24 km"}],"notes":[{"id":"travel-note-1","enabled":true,"text":"53 restaurants are within a 0.5km radius"},{"id":"travel-note-2","enabled":true,"text":"To Ubud 1h 20 minute (23 km) via Jl. By Pass Ngurah Rai"},{"id":"travel-note-3","enabled":true,"text":"To Seminyak 1h (16 km) via Jl. By Pass Ngurah Rai dan Jl. Sunset Road"},{"id":"travel-note-4","enabled":true,"text":"To Airport 37 minute (16 km) via Jl. By Pass Ngurah Rai"},{"id":"travel-note-5","enabled":true,"text":"To Canggu 1h 19 minute (20 km) via Jl. Raya Canggu"}],"newsletter":{"enabled":false,"referenceDemoVisual":true,"eyebrow":"Join Us","heading":"Sign up to hear the latest from Tandjung Sari","image":{"src":"/reference-location/52b0da91d4b79d632f79.webp","alt":"Postcard lettering and a red flower","category":"Nature","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"fieldLabel":"Email","actionLabel":"Sign Up"}},"signaturePackages":{"title":"Packages & Activities","description":"The small town of Sanur offers a picturesque coastal area and nearby attractions. At Tandjung Sari, where the beach is attentively nurtured, guests are invited to experience Sanur at its finest, aligning with the idea of \"A Magical Door to Bali.\"","hero":{"src":"/reference-packages/9c265899db00b1a62b1a.webp","alt":"Sanur beachfront shaded by palm trees","category":"Living","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"sections":[{"id":"sanur-editorial-introduction","enabled":true,"layout":"editorialIntro","heading":"The small town of Sanur offers a picturesque coastal area and nearby attractions. At Tandjung Sari, where the beach is attentively nurtured, guests are invited to experience Sanur at its finest, aligning with the idea of \"A Magical Door to Bali.\"","body":"To enhance our guests' experience, we offer a range of curated packages and activities designed for your leisure and deepen your understanding of the creativity-inspiring Balinese art and culture.","small":{"src":"/reference-packages/96732e8615db3b0453d3.webp","alt":"Balinese palm decorations in warm evening light","category":"Living","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"tall":{"src":"/reference-packages/e7211d4ab58b4c68ee1b.webp","alt":"Pool and garden viewed through the trees","category":"Living","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}}}]},"signatureTerms":{"enabled":true,"title":"Terms & Conditions","description":"Reference-demo policy text for visual comparison only.","sections":[{"id":"general-terms-and-conditions","enabled":true,"title":"GENERAL TERMS & CONDITIONS","compactIntroduction":false,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"All rates we quote are, of course, subject to availability and alteration."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"All special offers quoted are limited and subject to availability, and may be subject to a minimum stay."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"While every effort has been made to ensure the accuracy of all information, Tandjung Sari Hotel cannot accept liability for any errors or omissions and we reserve the right to change information and descriptions to amend manifest error in the quoted prices."}]},{"id":"online-bookings","enabled":true,"title":"ONLINE BOOKINGS","compactIntroduction":false,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Please note that different terms, conditions and cancellation policies in relation to online booking via Tandjung Sari Hotel website may apply, depending on the room or rate and package type chosen."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Please read the room rate details that are provided carefully before you make your online booking."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Once your booking is made, you will receive an on-screen confirmation reference number – we recommend you make a note of it, though you will also receive an email outlining your reference number and reservation details. In the event that you have to cancel your reservation, you will need your confirmation reference number, as well as the email address used to make the reservation."}]},{"id":"guaranteed-reservations","enabled":true,"title":"GUARANTEED RESERVATIONS","compactIntroduction":false,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Credit card details are taken at the time of booking for guarantee purposes. By securing your online reservation with a credit card, your room is guaranteed until midnight on the day of arrival, after which the room is released and may be resold. All reservations made on www.tandjungsarihotel.com must be guaranteed with a major credit card (Visa, MasterCard, American Express). In the case of a no show, your credit card will be charged depending on the room or rate and package type chosen."}]},{"id":"early-bird-and-last-minute-rate","enabled":true,"title":"EARLY BIRD & LAST MINUTE RATE","compactIntroduction":false,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"When booking an Advance Purchase Rate your credit card will be charged for the entire stay at the time of booking and the cost is completely non-refundable. A cancellation or change will result in forfeit of the cost of the reservation."}]},{"id":"cancellations","enabled":true,"title":"CANCELLATIONS","compactIntroduction":false,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Cancellations must be made within the cancellation period signified on the reservation confirmation. If notice of cancellation is not received by the required date, the hotel will charge one night's accommodation. Please note that some rates (e.g. Early Bird and Last Minute Rates) are non-refundable and in the event of a no show, the full charge of the booking is taken from your credit card."}]},{"id":"promotions-and-offers","enabled":true,"title":"PROMOTIONS AND OFFERS","compactIntroduction":false,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"All promotional offers are subject to specific terms, conditions and restrictions listed on each promotions and offers. All special offers are subject to availability."}]},{"id":"pricing-errors","enabled":true,"title":"PRICING ERRORS","compactIntroduction":true,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Tandjung Sari Hotel reserves the right to cancel contracts based upon incorrect information having been displayed in relation to price or service."}]},{"id":"limitations-to-liability","enabled":true,"title":"LIMITATIONS TO LIABILITY","compactIntroduction":false,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"In no event shall Tandjung Sari Hotel be liable for any direct, special, indirect or consequential damage or damages arising out of your access or use, or your inability to use Tandjung Sari Hotel website, or any materials or recommendations made by third parties on Tandjung Sari Hotel."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"You hereby waive any and all claims against us arising out of your use of our website or any materials or recommendations of any third parties on our website."}]},{"id":"warranty-disclaimer","enabled":true,"title":"WARRANTY DISCLAIMER","compactIntroduction":false,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"The content of Tandjung Sari Hotel website is provided \"as is\" without warranties of any kind, implied or expressed, statutory or otherwise, including without limitation, the warranties of merchantability or fitness for a particular purpose. Tandjung Sari Hotel also does not warrant the accuracy or completeness of the information, links or graphics found on Tandjung Sari Hotel website. Tandjung Sari Hotel may make changes to the content or policies at any time without prior notice."}]},{"id":"children-policy","enabled":true,"title":"CHILDREN POLICY","compactIntroduction":false,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Tandjung Sari Hotel is well-known for its tranquil surroundings. Therefore, if you are traveling with children, we respectfully ask for your help to ensure that your children can also enjoy being welcome here by not playing roughly and shouting, especially if they are in the vicinity of public areas such as the restaurant, pool and beach, so that our other guests can also feel comfortable."}]}]},"terms":"This is a fictional villa website demonstration. Images are illustrative and do not represent an actual property. Reservations, rates, cancellation policies, and availability must be confirmed directly with your host. No payments are collected on this website.","booking":{"controlsEnabled":false,"mode":"external","whatsapp":"","url":"https://example.com","message":"Hello {villa}, I would like to enquire about {room}."},"showAdminLink":true,"showCmsLinkInNavigation":true}$seed$::jsonb, "published" = $seed${"contentVersion":1,"name":"Tandjung Sari","tagline":"A private retreat in Bali","heroTitle":"Our Story","intro":"Beyond the rush, beneath the palms. A small collection of private villas made for slow mornings, unhurried conversations, and the simple pleasure of feeling at home.","storyTitle":"Rooted in Bali. Made for you.","story":"Sodai began with a simple idea: make room for the things that matter. The sound of water. A meal shared slowly. A garden that changes with the light.\n\nOur fictional villa collection celebrates the island’s natural rhythm through open spaces, honest materials, and thoughtful hospitality. This is an illustrative website demo, rather than a real property listing.","storyPanels":[{"id":"beginning","enabled":true,"layout":"intro","title":"A slower beginning","body":["A place begins with a feeling. At Sodai, that feeling is the calm of arriving among palms, with the day still open before you."],"images":[{"src":"/images/nature.jpg","alt":"Sunlight over a Balinese landscape","category":"Nature"}],"caption":"An imagined retreat in Bali"},{"id":"island-fragments","enabled":true,"layout":"archive","title":"Collected moments","body":["Morning light, familiar materials, and a path that turns toward the garden."],"images":[{"src":"/images/beach.jpg","alt":"A quiet tropical shoreline under a blue sky","category":"Nature"},{"src":"/images/living.jpg","alt":"A warm, airy living room with natural materials","category":"Living"},{"src":"/images/pool.jpg","alt":"A tranquil blue swimming pool surrounded by palms","category":"Spaces"}],"caption":"Scenes from the fictional Sodai collection"},{"id":"thoughtful-spaces","enabled":true,"layout":"editorial","title":"Room to pause","body":["We imagined spaces with generous openings and quiet corners. Each villa invites the outdoors in, while leaving enough privacy to feel entirely at home.","The story is told in simple gestures: cool water after a warm day, a shaded seat, a table set for an unhurried meal."],"images":[{"src":"/images/room.jpg","alt":"A spacious bedroom with soft linen and natural light","category":"Living"}],"caption":"Soft light and natural textures"},{"id":"unhurried-rhythm","enabled":true,"layout":"quote","title":"Let the day unfold in its own time.","body":["There is no prescribed way to be here. Follow the light, rest awhile, and discover your own rhythm."],"images":[],"caption":""},{"id":"shared-table","enabled":true,"layout":"split","title":"Gather, then linger","body":["Breakfast can stretch into conversation. Later, the garden becomes a place to return to before the evening begins.","Our fictional hospitality is built around giving guests time and space, with thoughtful help close at hand."],"images":[{"src":"/images/dining.jpg","alt":"Thoughtfully prepared food served in a restaurant","category":"Living"},{"src":"/images/nature.jpg","alt":"Sunlight over a Balinese landscape","category":"Nature"}],"caption":"The pleasure of an open afternoon"},{"id":"island-culture","enabled":true,"layout":"culture","title":"A living island","body":["Bali's traditions belong to its communities. We invite visitors to approach them with curiosity, respect, and guidance from local hosts.","Its arts, ceremonies, and daily offerings make space for reflection beyond the villa walls."],"images":[{"src":"/images/beach.jpg","alt":"A quiet tropical shoreline under a blue sky","category":"Nature"}],"caption":"Explore Culture Bali"},{"id":"new-perspectives","enabled":true,"layout":"collage","title":"Always becoming","body":["The landscape changes with the hour. A familiar view feels new in rain, in morning haze, or just before dusk.","Sodai is a fictional villa demonstration, yet its invitation is real: notice the details and stay a little longer."],"images":[{"src":"/images/suite.jpg","alt":"A comfortable suite with a generous bed","category":"Living"},{"src":"/images/pool.jpg","alt":"A tranquil blue swimming pool surrounded by palms","category":"Spaces"},{"src":"/images/living.jpg","alt":"A warm, airy living room with natural materials","category":"Living"}],"caption":"Different corners, one gentle pace"},{"id":"stay-with-us","enabled":true,"layout":"closing","title":"Come as you are. Leave with time to remember.","body":["Whether you seek solitude or time together, this imagined place is here to show how a stay can feel personal.","Turn the page and find your own space."],"images":[{"src":"/images/hero.jpg","alt":"A palm-lined tropical resort with a turquoise swimming pool","category":"Spaces"}],"caption":"Sodai · an illustrative villa collection"},{"id":"a-moment-between","enabled":true,"layout":"cinematic","title":"A moment between places","body":["Where the shore meets the light, let the story linger a little longer."],"images":[{"src":"/images/beach.jpg","alt":"A quiet tropical shoreline under a blue sky","category":"Nature"}],"caption":"An image-led pause in the fictional villa story"}],"foundation":{"enabled":true,"title":"The Foundation","description":"Bali stands as a beacon of rich cultural and artistic heritage, shaped by its vibrant population and noble traditions.","hero":{"src":"/reference-foundation/e70b58d850d16896b569.webp","alt":"Balinese dance lesson at the Tandjung Sari Foundation","category":"Spaces","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"sections":[{"id":"cultural-heritage","enabled":true,"layout":"heritage","heading":"Bali stands as a beacon of rich cultural and artistic heritage, shaped by its vibrant population and noble traditions.","archive":{"src":"/reference-foundation/29792a3478d01a6fa914.webp","alt":"Archival Balinese dancers","category":"Spaces","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"caption":"Renowned for its resilience against colonial forces, the island embodies a paradise that fiercely preserves its unique identity within Indonesia.","statement":"Yet, a reputation—regardless of its accuracy—cannot alone uphold a culture; a strong foundation of support is essential.","body":["As Bali transforms in the face of rapid tourism development, traditional institutions that have historically supported Balinese culture must adapt. Without innovative support, such as private and corporate patronage, the island risks losing its profound aesthetic values and cultural identity.","In response to this challenge, the Tandjung Sari Foundation was established in 1987 by the visionary Wawo-Runtu family, owners of the Tandjung Sari Hotel. The foundation is dedicated to the preservation and evolution of Balinese artistic works of exceptional quality."],"teacher":{"src":"/reference-foundation/6f59373a48bf2c7aace1.webp","alt":"A teacher guiding a child through a traditional dance lesson","category":"Spaces","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}}},{"id":"traditional-knowledge","enabled":true,"layout":"commitment","heading":"With a commitment to recover and promote traditional knowledge, the Tanjung Sari Foundation upholds high standards of artistic expression across fine arts, applied arts, and performing arts.","small":{"src":"/reference-foundation/7f0b73715e344302aaf5.webp","alt":"Children practising Balinese dance outdoors","category":"Spaces","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"portrait":{"src":"/reference-foundation/6d3deb49f2e19071f138.webp","alt":"A child practising a dance gesture with a fan","category":"Spaces","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"statement":"It nurtures creativity by merging traditional values with contemporary forms of expression."},{"id":"foundation-aims","enabled":true,"layout":"aims","heading":"The Foundation’s Aims:","entries":[{"id":"celebrate-artists","enabled":true,"body":"Identify and celebrate outstanding artists who embody high artistic standards and their representative works."},{"id":"document-artistry","enabled":true,"body":"Document their artistry through various mediums, including video, audio recordings, photography, and written records."}]},{"id":"dance-lesson-panorama","enabled":true,"layout":"widePhoto","image":{"src":"/reference-foundation/34761eefca21682077af.webp","alt":"Children practising dance together on a wooden floor","category":"Spaces","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}}},{"id":"initial-programs","enabled":true,"layout":"programs","heading":"The foundation’s initial programs have breathed new life into the performing arts, revitalizing local banjar activities —","statement":"the heart of community life, where children learn to dance and where the soulful sounds of gamelan resonate.","decoration":{"src":"/reference-story/rail-emblem.svg","alt":"Coral motif","category":"Spaces"},"entries":[{"id":"banjar-sindhu","enabled":true,"image":{"src":"/reference-foundation/7d590921ccb8cf8e06ba.webp","alt":"Banjar Sindhu gamelan musicians","category":"Spaces","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"description":"By restoring the Banjar Sindhu gamelan group and providing traditional instruments for the rare Gamelan Semar Pegulingan, the foundation is reigniting a powerful musical legacy.","placement":"low"},{"id":"traditional-teachers","enabled":true,"image":{"src":"/reference-foundation/11bd3c2f938f74942b06.webp","alt":"A dance teacher sharing traditional gestures","category":"Spaces","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"description":"Esteemed artists inspired over one hundred local children and trainee teachers, imparting time-honored standards of excellence. They taught a range of traditional works, ensuring that these vital expressions are not lost to time.","placement":"high"},{"id":"oral-visual-history","enabled":true,"image":{"src":"/reference-foundation/8cfc4e1e57f2bc85b28c.webp","alt":"Children preparing for a ceremony","category":"Spaces","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"description":"As teachers shared their wisdom, they contributed to an “oral and visual history,” recording their knowledge of music, instruments, dance, and the intricate arts of costuming and palm leaf decoration.","placement":"low"},{"id":"student-performances","enabled":true,"image":{"src":"/reference-foundation/27dd153c77402d97bf5f.webp","alt":"Young dancers at a student performance","category":"Spaces","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"description":"The foundation also sponsors student performances, reintroducing these artistic standards to the community.","placement":"high"}]},{"id":"current-initiatives","enabled":true,"layout":"initiatives","heading":"Current initiatives focus on inspiring the community through the performing arts.","small":{"src":"/reference-foundation/e9b49fd06e586ada1297.webp","alt":"A young dancer performing in Balinese costume","category":"Spaces","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"wide":{"src":"/reference-foundation/fbe2f568a96225b92f24.webp","alt":"Balinese dancers performing together in the evening","category":"Spaces","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"portrait":{"src":"/reference-foundation/0525788b2077beba39f2.webp","alt":"A Baris dancer in elaborate traditional costume","category":"Spaces","focalPoint":{"x":50,"y":50}},"statement":"The Tandjung Sari Foundation proudly sponsors classical Balinese dance lessons for local children,","body":"offering enriching tutoring sessions twice a week on Friday and Sunday afternoons from 3:30 pm to 5:00 pm at Tandjung Sari.Furthermore, a cultural evening showcasing the talents of these children through classical Balinese dance is held every first and third Saturday of the month.","closing":"To support the preservation of these art forms, please consider making a donation to Yayasan Tandjung Bali Sari at Bank Mandiri, using account number 1450016111375 and swift code BMRIIDJA."}]},"signatureMenu":{"logo":{"src":"/reference-story/menu-logo.svg","alt":"Tandjung Sari — cape of flowers","category":"Spaces"},"photo":{"src":"/reference-story/lobby-editwebp.webp","alt":"Tandjung Sari's carved wooden lobby","category":"Spaces"},"referenceLabels":true,"introBrand":{"emblem":{"src":"/reference-story/intro-emblem.svg","alt":"Brand coral emblem","category":"Spaces"},"wordmark":{"src":"/reference-story/intro-wordmark.svg","alt":"Tandjung Sari wordmark","category":"Spaces"},"aspectRatio":1.0133333333333334,"emblemBounds":{"x":0.4605,"y":32.4,"width":66.0526,"height":66.9333}},"contactTitle":"Get in Touch","social":[],"legal":"© 2026 Sodai. Reference comparison demo.","credit":"Website by Sodai"},"signatureStory":{"railEmblem":{"src":"/reference-story/rail-emblem.svg","alt":"Tandjung Sari coral emblem","category":"Spaces"},"nextPageTitle":"Our Rooms","sections":[{"id":"story-opener","enabled":true,"layout":"opener","title":"Our Story","image":{"src":"/reference-story/lobby-editwebp.webp","alt":"Tandjung Sari's carved wooden lobby","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"the-1960s","enabled":true,"layout":"intro","eyebrow":"Initiated in the","date":"1960’s,","body":"Tandjung Sari's logo evolved from a coral shot in front of Tandjung Sari beach, which Hans Hoefer presented to Wija as a full-page ad in the first guidebook to Bali printed in 1970. The logo practically \"designed itself\" as an extension of that shot","logo":{"src":"/reference-story/home-story-logo.svg","alt":"Tandjung Sari coral emblem","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"sanur-timeline","enabled":true,"layout":"timeline","leadImage":{"src":"/reference-story/1960c-1jpg.jpeg","alt":"Archival photograph of the early Tandjung Sari house","category":"Spaces"},"entries":[{"id":"pax-neerlandica","image":{"src":"/reference-story/pak-wija-1-1jpg.jpeg","alt":"Archival photograph of Wija at a table","category":"Spaces"},"body":"Tourism in Bali started during the Pax Neerlandica (1908–1942) under the strict control of the Dutch colonial government after their final conquest of the island."},{"id":"sanur-hotels","image":{"src":"/reference-story/1960b-1jpg.jpeg","alt":"Archival Sanur shoreline with boats","category":"Spaces"},"body":"In time, Sanur evolved into a prominent tourist destination with the construction of the Segara Beach Hotel (which became the Segara Village) and later with the building of the InterContinental’s Bali Beach Hotel with Japanese war reparations."},{"id":"early-1960s","image":{"src":"/reference-story/timeline-interior.jpg","alt":"Archival Tandjung Sari interior with staff beneath the lamps","category":"Spaces"},"body":"If you conjure Sanur in the early 1960s when the Tandjung Sari was born, the vision you get will be a quiet one. The beach then was nearly deserted during the day, except for the coming and going of fishermen in their bright little boats and, at low tide, the harvesting of coral from the lagoon's protective reef."}],"finalImage":{"src":"/reference-story/resize-2jpg.jpeg","alt":"Early Tandjung Sari bungalow among palms","category":"Spaces"}},{"id":"founding","enabled":true,"layout":"founding","heading":"The Tandjung Sari did not intend to become the seminal boutique hotel of tropical Asia.","body":["It began as a place to spend the night for its owner, Wija Wawo-Runtu (1926 - 2001), and his family when they visited Bali from Jakarta on shopping trips for their antique business.","The Wawo-Runtu's little paradise attracted friends from Jakarta, and by 1962, they had four small bungalows for friends who wished to visit Bali.","Within a few years, Tandjung Sari was internationally renowned among smart people as the place to stay if you could get in."],"image":{"src":"/reference-story/resize-3jpg.jpeg","alt":"Tandjung Sari's beachfront terrace","category":"Spaces"},"rightHeading":"Bali's tourism industry began to flourish, leading to the expansion of the island's international airport, which was officially inaugurated as Bali International Airport Ngurah Rai in August 1969.","insetImage":{"src":"/reference-story/frame-38608png.png","alt":"Archival view of Sanur's tourism development","category":"Spaces"},"rightCaption":"As tourism continued to grow, Sanur became the most prestigious address on the island."},{"id":"intimacy-with-bali","enabled":true,"layout":"redEditorial","image":{"src":"/reference-story/resize-1jpg.jpeg","alt":"Red-toned photograph of traditional Balinese architecture","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"Wija understood that visitors wanted intimacy with Bali.","body":["They wanted to feel the air of Bali on their skin and to live in what they imagined was a Balinese way but more comfortably."],"alignment":"low"},{"id":"batujimbar-estate","enabled":true,"layout":"architecture","image":{"src":"/reference-story/15-1png.png","alt":"Two archival photographs of Tandjung Sari architecture","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"The success of the Tandjung Sari convinced him that the concept could be taken to a larger scale.","caption":"That inspired the development of the Batujimbar Estate.","body":["In February 1974, Indonesia hosted the Pacific Asia Travel Association (PATA) conference, and a few months earlier, in October 1973, Bali Hyatt was completed.","On a par with the expanded Tandjung Sari, with its sixteen new bungalows normally full, the restaurant was a powerful magnet, too. The Tandjung Sari's famous cuisine captivated Craig Claiborne, a food writer and former editor of The New York Times, who devoted a chapter to Tatie Wawo-Runtu's recipe for Soto Ayam.","When the structures were still new and the hotel was doing very well, there were lots of celebrated guests: Calvin Klein, Kirk Douglas, David Bowie, Mick Jagger, Queen Ingrid of Denmark, Margaret Mead, Ingrid Bergman, Annie Lennox, Ringo Starr, Yoko Ono, Paul Getty Jr. and his wife Talitha, and Lionel Poilâne."]},{"id":"cultural-performance","enabled":true,"layout":"redEditorial","image":{"src":"/reference-story/snapinstaapp27269686895319103558308643829194325254783n1080-1png.png","alt":"Young Balinese dancers in gold performance dress","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"The Tandjung Sari cultural performance has significantly contributed to the place's legend.","body":["Numerous cultural activities were initiated, and the Tandjung Sari Foundation was established in September 1987 to formalize the commitment to preserve classical dance and other aspects of Balinese culture.","Dance lessons are still regularly scheduled on Friday and Sunday afternoons to tutor children from the local banjar, and their performances take place on stage every first and third Saturday evening of the month."],"alignment":"high"},{"id":"gentle-renaissance","enabled":true,"layout":"laterHistory","image":{"src":"/reference-story/20220726133315-1jpg.jpeg","alt":"Vintage vehicle outside Tandjung Sari","category":"Spaces"},"decoration":{"src":"/reference-story/later-emblem.svg","alt":"Coral motif","category":"Spaces"},"heading":"For years, the hotel had been coasting from the boom years of the 1970s and '80s, shocked by the impact of the 1991 Gulf War, the 1997 financial crisis, Wija Wawo-Runtu's passing, and the 2003 SARS epidemic.","note":"Then came the gentle renaissance. In 2005, the Tandjung Sari underwent its first renovations","detailImage":{"src":"/reference-story/pillar-ornamentsjpg.jpeg","alt":"Carved Balinese architectural pillar","category":"Spaces"},"bookHeading":"At the age of fifty in 2012, the hotel was deeply rejuvenated from within. To celebrate the golden anniversary of Tandjung Sari, the remarkable book Tandjung Sari—A Magical Door to Bali was launched.","body":["The book tells how the hotel grew, the challenges and triumphs, and the people who made it happen. The book has become known for telling the early '60s tourism story in Sanur and enticing readers to dig more into Balinese architecture.","Another step of the 55-year milestone (2017) was celebrated with the Tandjung Sari documentary film, which portrayed the journey from its early days."]},{"id":"a-magical-door","enabled":true,"layout":"bookClosing","image":{"src":"/reference-story/dsc06901-1png.png","alt":"Tandjung Sari: A Magical Door to Bali book","category":"Spaces"},"body":["What drew people was the Tandjung Sari's judicious blend of the lowkey and luxurious. The architecture was simple, using local materials and Balinese building techniques, yet the location was on a prime beachfront with wonderful gardens. The rooms were furnished with Balinese antiques, and the hospitality was warm and sophisticated.","Guests felt they were experiencing a highly refined version of \"the real Bali\" with all its sounds and silences, deep perfumes, bare-handedness and hilarity, and powerful enchantment at the edge of a spangled sea."],"heading":"The Tandjung Sari remains a treasure today, still run by the Wawo-Runtu family, discreet and elegantly modest, an ageless beauty."},{"enabled":false,"source":"","poster":null,"id":"documentary-still","layout":"video"}],"video":{"enabled":false,"source":"","poster":null}},"culture":{"enabled":true,"hero":{"src":"/reference-culture/ab393444c4123aa8c18b.webp","alt":"Balinese ceremonial procession","category":"Living"},"title":"Cultures","introTitle":"Bali, with its enchanting charm, presents a tapestry of unique and authentic cultural experiences waiting to be discovered across the island.","intro":["Some are just around the corner, while others invite you to embark on an adventure, requiring a tour or transportation to reach their distant beauty.","The Balinese cultural calendar, following the Saka/local calendar, unfolds throughout the year, offering a journey of inspiration and wonder."],"introImages":[{"src":"/reference-culture/0b53fbd7e1c7785fafe7.webp","alt":"Map of Bali","category":"Living"},{"src":"/reference-culture/80456c8e17d1b49c9da0.webp","alt":"Balinese ceremonial carving","category":"Living"}],"entries":[{"id":"galungan","enabled":true,"slug":"galungan","title":"Galungan","summary":"The Galungan holiday, one of Bali’s most important, falls once every 210 days, in the Balinese week of Dunggulan, always on a Wednesday.","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/d1861ff92e521db9b46a.webp","alt":"Galungan","category":"Living"},"heading":"The essence of Galungan is to defeat evil in oneself so that we can live in peace and harmony.","body":["According to old written records, Galungan was first celebrated on the 15th full moon of the year 804 in the Balinese Saka calendar, or 882 AD, to honor the triumph of Lord Indra over the evil king Mayadenawa, seen as a victory of good over evil. The term Galungan comes from Old Javanese and means ‘battle, combat’."],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-culture/d1861ff92e521db9b46a.webp","alt":"Galungan","category":"Living"},"nextSlug":"kuningan-and-mekotek","sections":[{"id":"galungan-portrait-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"portraitEditorial","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/e0b55b7a8293115c0db1.webp","alt":"Galungan editorial photograph","category":"Living"},"heading":"The essence of Galungan is to defeat evil in oneself so that we can live in peace and harmony.","body":["According to old written records, Galungan was first celebrated on the 15th full moon of the year 804 in the Balinese Saka calendar, or 882 AD, to honor the triumph of Lord Indra over the evil king Mayadenawa, seen as a victory of good over evil. The term Galungan comes from Old Javanese and means ‘battle, combat’."]},{"id":"galungan-red-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"redOverlay","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/dfe0b83899ba31583d4f.webp","alt":"Galungan cultural ceremony","category":"Living"},"heading":"On Galungan day, the island takes on an even more magical atmosphere","body":["with the towering penjor (decorated bamboo poles) standing at the gate of every house.","The Balinese believe that the spirits of the ancestors return home during Galungan. Therefore, prayers and offerings are prepared to welcome the spirits."]}]}},{"id":"kuningan-and-mekotek","enabled":true,"slug":"kuningan-and-mekotek","title":"Kuningan & Mekotek","summary":"Kuningan is a Balinese holy day celebrated ten days after Galungan. It derives from ka-uningan, meaning wisdom, and the ritual aim is to attain spiritual elevation through introspection.","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/5b7d0c5e7dac9045e6e5.webp","alt":"Kuningan & Mekotek","category":"Living"},"heading":"Kuningan is a Balinese holy day celebrated ten days after Galungan.","body":["On Kuningan day, we can witness an unusual rite called mekotekan in the village of Munggu, once the seat of the powerful kingdom of Mengwi. In this purification ritual, the young men of the village each carry a pole, from two to 3.5 meters long, made of pulet wood. They process around the village to the temple Pura Luhur Beten Bingin, where they pile the poles together to create a pyramid-like construction, in which teams compete to climb."],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-culture/5b7d0c5e7dac9045e6e5.webp","alt":"Kuningan & Mekotek","category":"Living"},"nextSlug":"melasti","sections":[{"id":"kuningan-and-mekotek-portrait-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"portraitEditorial","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/3d18647fe94d9db35207.webp","alt":"Kuningan & Mekotek editorial photograph","category":"Living"},"heading":"Kuningan is a Balinese holy day celebrated ten days after Galungan.","body":["On Kuningan day, we can witness an unusual rite called mekotekan in the village of Munggu, once the seat of the powerful kingdom of Mengwi. In this purification ritual, the young men of the village each carry a pole, from two to 3.5 meters long, made of pulet wood. They process around the village to the temple Pura Luhur Beten Bingin, where they pile the poles together to create a pyramid-like construction, in which teams compete to climb."]},{"id":"kuningan-and-mekotek-red-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"redOverlay","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/a03e07274ca0e02df89f.webp","alt":"Kuningan & Mekotek cultural ceremony","category":"Living"},"heading":"As the sticks crash together, they make a sound like tek tek tek, thus the term mekotekan.","body":["The rite is said to have roots in the victory of Mengwi over Blambangan in East Java in the 17th century. It is held to honor ancestral heroes, and with the hope of protection from unexpected misfortune."]}]}},{"id":"nyepi","enabled":true,"slug":"nyepi","title":"Nyepi","summary":"The Balinese New Year is known as Nyepi and is celebrated according to the Saka lunar calendar, on the dark of the moon of the spring equinox, usually falling in March or early April.","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/90ff749fbcbbd0df686d.webp","alt":"Nyepi","category":"Living"},"heading":"The word nyepi comes from ‘sepi’, meaning ‘empty’.","body":["Although Nyepi is a traditional Balinese Hindu celebration, it has become a national holiday in Indonesia. The folk idea is to make the world appear as if deserted, so that disruptive spirits will abandon the island and look elsewhere to cause mischief."],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-culture/90ff749fbcbbd0df686d.webp","alt":"Nyepi","category":"Living"},"nextSlug":"piodalan","sections":[{"id":"nyepi-portrait-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"portraitEditorial","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/f2dbeec750059c34c5e5.webp","alt":"Nyepi editorial photograph","category":"Living"},"heading":"The word nyepi comes from ‘sepi’, meaning ‘empty’.","body":["Although Nyepi is a traditional Balinese Hindu celebration, it has become a national holiday in Indonesia. The folk idea is to make the world appear as if deserted, so that disruptive spirits will abandon the island and look elsewhere to cause mischief."]},{"id":"nyepi-red-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"redOverlay","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/a859db4cc69dde54c8db.webp","alt":"Nyepi cultural ceremony","category":"Living"},"heading":"There is no traffic on the roads, and in the evening, lights are not to be turned on. Ngurah Rai Airport is closed to all flights.","body":["On Nyepi, everyone is asked to stay inside their\nhome compound for 24 hours, from dawn to the following dawn. Visitors, too,\nmust comply with this custom and are asked not to stray from the hotel grounds.Many visitors remark on the extraordinary quiet and peacefulness of this day of silence.","The Balinese people treat Nyepi as an opportunity to meditate and fast. The importance of this holy day is to detach oneself from the world and seek inward peace."]}]}},{"id":"melasti","enabled":true,"slug":"melasti","title":"Melasti","summary":"Three days before Nyepi, a large purification\nceremony called melasti is held by villages all over Bali.","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/ab5435506ce86cc67fa9.webp","alt":"Melasti","category":"Living"},"heading":"The sea is a significant element for Balinese Hindus, who believe that it is the realm where all spiritual impurities are destroyed.","body":["Each household erects a triangular altar for\nofferings by the roadside, and holy objects from the temples are brought in\nprocession to the sea to be cleansed in a special ritual.","Massive community processions gather on beaches\nall around the island to participate in this ritual cleansing. Guests can witness this inspiring ceremony on Sanur Beach."],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-culture/ab5435506ce86cc67fa9.webp","alt":"Melasti","category":"Living"},"nextSlug":"ogoh-ogoh","sections":[{"id":"melasti-portrait-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"portraitEditorial","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/7e5c7ef865bbd2c6bfc9.webp","alt":"Melasti editorial photograph","category":"Living"},"heading":"The sea is a significant element for Balinese Hindus, who believe that it is the realm where all spiritual impurities are destroyed.","body":["Each household erects a triangular altar for\nofferings by the roadside, and holy objects from the temples are brought in\nprocession to the sea to be cleansed in a special ritual.","Massive community processions gather on beaches\nall around the island to participate in this ritual cleansing. Guests can witness this inspiring ceremony on Sanur Beach."]},{"id":"melasti-red-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"redOverlay","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/f9c2fa78bbd9daac70fe.webp","alt":"Melasti cultural ceremony","category":"Living"},"heading":"Guests can witness this inspiring ceremony on Sanur Beach.","body":["Hindus people believe that it is the realm where all spiritual impurities are destroyed. Massive community processions gather on beaches all around the island to participate in this ritual cleansing."]}]}},{"id":"ogoh-ogoh","enabled":true,"slug":"ogoh-ogoh","title":"Ogoh-ogoh","summary":"In the evening of Pengrupukan, the day before\nNyepi, villages parade ogoh-ogoh—giant effigies of demons, designed and\nbuilt by the youth of each community.","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/b80d8290bd0c4d05b2ef.webp","alt":"Ogoh-ogoh","category":"Living"},"heading":"The ogoh-ogoh parade is intense—noisy and wild, accompanied by torches and orchestras of cymbals and gongs.","body":["In household ceremonies, the people will bang\ngongs, pots and pans, and bamboo sticks to chase the evil spirits from the\nisland.","It takes place in village streets and centers. Traditionally, the procession ends up at the cemetery where the effigies are burned, and all the negative energies are dispersed, preparing the way for the peace of Nyepi."],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-culture/b80d8290bd0c4d05b2ef.webp","alt":"Ogoh-ogoh","category":"Living"},"nextSlug":"nyepi","sections":[{"id":"ogoh-ogoh-portrait-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"portraitEditorial","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/dcd762c7cf9356097560.webp","alt":"Ogoh-ogoh editorial photograph","category":"Living"},"heading":"The ogoh-ogoh parade is intense—noisy and wild, accompanied by torches and orchestras of cymbals and gongs.","body":["In household ceremonies, the people will bang\ngongs, pots and pans, and bamboo sticks to chase the evil spirits from the\nisland.","It takes place in village streets and centers. Traditionally, the procession ends up at the cemetery where the effigies are burned, and all the negative energies are dispersed, preparing the way for the peace of Nyepi."]},{"id":"ogoh-ogoh-red-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"redOverlay","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/0079bad9b0beec2dfd26.webp","alt":"Ogoh-ogoh cultural ceremony","category":"Living"},"heading":"Creating an ogoh-ogoh—usually from bamboo, wood, and paper—takes two to three months and involves all the men in the banjar, or community unit.","body":["Some ogoh-ogoh have mechanized movements. Every year there is creative suspense to see what new forms will emerge and what materials are used. Recently there was a trend for dried banana leaves and used plastic bottles."]}]}},{"id":"piodalan","enabled":true,"slug":"piodalan","title":"Piodalan","summary":"A piodalan is a temple’s anniversary,\nwhen the deities are believed to come down from heaven to the temple shrines,\npartake of offerings, and convey blessings through the medium of holy water.","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/cf5a2c6bca0d3d5f8372.webp","alt":"Piodalan","category":"Living"},"heading":"Temple anniversaries date from their founding and occur all around the year, whether on the 210-day Balinese calendar or the Saka lunar calendar.","body":["The gods are welcomed with offerings of food, flowers, traditional music, and dances. People wear their best temple clothes, and it is a very happy time."],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-culture/cf5a2c6bca0d3d5f8372.webp","alt":"Piodalan","category":"Living"},"nextSlug":"bali-art-festival","sections":[{"id":"piodalan-portrait-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"portraitEditorial","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/eb27cd01d7bac1b2fc45.webp","alt":"Piodalan editorial photograph","category":"Living"},"heading":"Temple anniversaries date from their founding and occur all around the year, whether on the 210-day Balinese calendar or the Saka lunar calendar.","body":["The gods are welcomed with offerings of food, flowers, traditional music, and dances. People wear their best temple clothes, and it is a very happy time."]},{"id":"piodalan-red-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"redOverlay","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/ff289cfb6703228b333f.webp","alt":"Piodalan cultural ceremony","category":"Living"},"heading":"The piodalan ceremony is also held at Pura Tandjung Sari—the beachfront temple for which the hotel is named—on Purnama Sasih Kedasa.","body":["Purnama sasih kedasa is the full moon of the tenth month of the Saka lunar calendar. It is a particularly holy day in Bali and usually falls in March or April.","You are welcome to witness this beautiful religious occasion. As with any Balinese ceremony, a sarong, and a sash, with a kebaya blouse for women, are required to be worn by those attending the ceremony."]}]}},{"id":"bali-art-festival","enabled":true,"slug":"bali-art-festival","title":"Bali Art Festival","summary":"The island’s largest and most spectacular\ncultural event, the Bali Arts Festival (Pesta Kesenian Bali), is an annual\nprogram organized by the government of Bali Province.","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/7403d9c7763d195fe7f5.webp","alt":"Bali Art Festival","category":"Living"},"heading":"The festival is held in Denpasar at the Werdhi Budaya Art Centre.","body":["It lasts for a month and takes place every year from mid-June to the middle of July. It showcases the variety and richness of\nperforming arts traditions from the different regions in Bali, as well as other\nprovinces in Indonesia and a number of foreign countries."],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-culture/7403d9c7763d195fe7f5.webp","alt":"Bali Art Festival","category":"Living"},"nextSlug":"perang-pandan-and-ayunan-jantra","sections":[{"id":"bali-art-festival-portrait-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"portraitEditorial","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/a83d7f3c72e417a26e15.webp","alt":"Bali Art Festival editorial photograph","category":"Living"},"heading":"The festival is held in Denpasar at the Werdhi Budaya Art Centre.","body":["It lasts for a month and takes place every year from mid-June to the middle of July. It showcases the variety and richness of\nperforming arts traditions from the different regions in Bali, as well as other\nprovinces in Indonesia and a number of foreign countries."]},{"id":"bali-art-festival-red-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"redOverlay","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/55b03ac5a999ba0999e7.webp","alt":"Bali Art Festival cultural ceremony","category":"Living"},"heading":"On the opening day, an enormous parade of all the performing groups is held in Renon, Denpasar.","body":["The festival is traditionally opened by the President of Indonesia."]}]}},{"id":"perang-pandan-and-ayunan-jantra","enabled":true,"slug":"perang-pandan-and-ayunan-jantra","title":"Perang Pandan & Ayunan Jantra","summary":"The Bali Aga village of Tenganan Dauh Tukad in Karangasem Regency has a unique tradition of a ritual battle with spiny pandan leaves, known as mekare-kare or mageret pandan.","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/d44b7226bb8f18301535.webp","alt":"Perang Pandan & Ayunan Jantra","category":"Living"},"heading":"The Perang Pandan ritual battle is carried out to honor the god Indra, the deity of war, and is part of the Sasih Sembah ceremonies, an important series of religious celebrations in Tenganan Village.","body":["This ceremony lasts for two days, held every fifth month or Sasih Kalima on Tenganan’s village calendar (around June)."],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-culture/d44b7226bb8f18301535.webp","alt":"Perang Pandan & Ayunan Jantra","category":"Living"},"nextSlug":"purnama-and-tilem","sections":[{"id":"perang-pandan-and-ayunan-jantra-portrait-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"portraitEditorial","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/f5dc41504a0b1b70bbd4.webp","alt":"Perang Pandan & Ayunan Jantra editorial photograph","category":"Living"},"heading":"The Perang Pandan ritual battle is carried out to honor the god Indra, the deity of war, and is part of the Sasih Sembah ceremonies, an important series of religious celebrations in Tenganan Village.","body":["This ceremony lasts for two days, held every fifth month or Sasih Kalima on Tenganan’s village calendar (around June)."]},{"id":"perang-pandan-and-ayunan-jantra-red-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"redOverlay","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/8e5c0cef5f24f749bad6.webp","alt":"Perang Pandan & Ayunan Jantra cultural ceremony","category":"Living"},"heading":"Following the Perang Pandan, the Ayunan Jantra (on a wooden circular swing) will grace the late afternoon.","body":["This tradition describes the continuous life cycle, inspiring young people to embrace the journey ahead. The swing’s ups and downs are a powerful reminder to prepare for the realities that await.","Please contact our reservations desk if you are interested in witnessing these cultural events."]}]}},{"id":"purnama-and-tilem","enabled":true,"slug":"purnama-and-tilem","title":"Purnama & Tilem","summary":"The full moon (Purnama) and the dark of the moon (Tilem) are always sacred days for Balinese Hindus.","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/121cce936dd20c4f007d.webp","alt":"Purnama & Tilem","category":"Living"},"heading":"Purnama is generally marked by a high tide.","body":["To protect the self from negative effects, people are advised to take time for introspection and self-purification."],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-culture/121cce936dd20c4f007d.webp","alt":"Purnama & Tilem","category":"Living"},"nextSlug":"offerings","sections":[{"id":"purnama-and-tilem-portrait-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"portraitEditorial","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/aef29ec2291b9a602257.webp","alt":"Purnama & Tilem editorial photograph","category":"Living"},"heading":"Purnama is generally marked by a high tide.","body":["To protect the self from negative effects, people are advised to take time for introspection and self-purification."]},{"id":"purnama-and-tilem-red-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"redOverlay","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/902e495f74f887d9d1e4.webp","alt":"Purnama & Tilem cultural ceremony","category":"Living"},"heading":"Tilem is the darkest night of the month.","body":["On Purnama and on Tilem, special offerings are placed in significant places around houses and temples and in local shrines everywhere.","Both stages of the moon are believed to have\nambivalent mystical energy."]}]}},{"id":"offerings","enabled":true,"slug":"offerings","title":"Offerings","summary":"In Bali, all religious rites, large and small, are carried out with offerings, called banten in Balinese.","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/b6dd788b515d2eeb761b.webp","alt":"Offerings","category":"Living"},"heading":"The knowledge of offerings is held by priestly families, and the art of making them is traditionally carried out by women, taught from one generation to the next.","body":["Most basically, these are symbolic amounts of food placed on a leaf container. But the variety of food and leaf containers—as well as the flowers and palm leaf ornaments, cut and pinned in myriad ways—is uncountably complex."],"signature":{"hero":{"src":"/reference-culture/b6dd788b515d2eeb761b.webp","alt":"Offerings","category":"Living"},"sections":[{"id":"offerings-portrait-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"portraitEditorial","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/1dda2b9e8893fc7ad095.webp","alt":"Offerings editorial photograph","category":"Living"},"heading":"The knowledge of offerings is held by priestly families, and the art of making them is traditionally carried out by women, taught from one generation to the next.","body":["Most basically, these are symbolic amounts of food placed on a leaf container. But the variety of food and leaf containers—as well as the flowers and palm leaf ornaments, cut and pinned in myriad ways—is uncountably complex."]},{"id":"offerings-red-editorial","enabled":true,"layout":"redOverlay","image":{"src":"/reference-culture/717c76a00ce0c9ee3369.webp","alt":"Offerings cultural ceremony","category":"Living"},"heading":"It is the profusion of offerings that give Bali its particular festive look and mystical feel.","body":["Each offering has a special form and meaning according to the custom of the particular place, and each one is offered with incense, holy water, and a prayer. And there is no room for improvisation.","Guests interested in learning Balinese offering-making can book through our reservations desk."]}]}}]},"address":"Ubud, Bali, Indonesia · illustrative location","email":"stay@example.com","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ubud+Bali","hero":{"src":"/reference-story/lobby-editwebp.webp","alt":"Tandjung Sari's carved wooden lobby","category":"Spaces"},"gallery":[{"src":"/images/hero.jpg","alt":"A palm-lined tropical resort with a turquoise swimming pool","category":"Spaces"},{"src":"/images/room.jpg","alt":"A spacious bedroom with soft linen and natural light","category":"Living"},{"src":"/images/pool.jpg","alt":"A tranquil blue swimming pool surrounded by palms","category":"Spaces"},{"src":"/images/living.jpg","alt":"A warm, airy living room with natural materials","category":"Living"},{"src":"/images/dining.jpg","alt":"Thoughtfully prepared food served in a restaurant","category":"Living"},{"src":"/images/nature.jpg","alt":"Sunlight over a Balinese landscape","category":"Nature"},{"src":"/images/beach.jpg","alt":"A quiet tropical shoreline under a blue sky","category":"Nature"},{"src":"/images/suite.jpg","alt":"A comfortable suite with a generous bed","category":"Living"}],"signatureGallery":{"enabled":true,"title":"Gallery","description":"Photographs of Tandjung Sari bungalows, dining, gardens and island life.","categories":[{"id":"bungalows","label":"Bungalows","enabled":true},{"id":"dining","label":"Dining","enabled":true}],"items":[{"id":"photo-04f0fe2c9de4be229f4b","enabled":true,"image":{"src":"/reference-gallery/04f0fe2c9de4be229f4b.webp","alt":"Shrimp and dumplings on a plate over grey timber","category":"Living"},"width":976,"height":549,"viewerOrder":65,"categories":["dining"]},{"id":"photo-c001d1deb663281f0733","enabled":true,"image":{"src":"/reference-gallery/c001d1deb663281f0733.webp","alt":"Dumplings and orange flowers on a white plate","category":"Living"},"width":549,"height":976,"viewerOrder":63,"categories":["dining"]},{"id":"photo-2bd1c5d15e5d3544d7b3","enabled":true,"image":{"src":"/reference-gallery/2bd1c5d15e5d3544d7b3.webp","alt":"Yellow rice cone and satay with orange flowers","category":"Living"},"width":549,"height":976,"viewerOrder":66,"categories":["dining"]},{"id":"photo-5e9f85bcca3c2ee9a3de","enabled":true,"image":{"src":"/reference-gallery/5e9f85bcca3c2ee9a3de.webp","alt":"Green salad and Parmesan in a green bowl","category":"Living"},"width":976,"height":549,"viewerOrder":68,"categories":["dining"]},{"id":"photo-b7346f44eb1f9f39e8b3","enabled":true,"image":{"src":"/reference-g